hey David do you see the offensive new  use of nuclear weapons happening during  your lifetime okay this question could  we could go on for an hour about this  but to sort of sum up my view I'm going  to take a sort of naive perspective I  admit it might be naive I don't think we  will see the use of offensive nuclear  weapons during my lifetime now when I  say this I don't mean that there will be  no offensive use of extremely powerful  weapons during my lifetime what I mean  is more of a technological argument  which is that dirty bombs that are far  less powerful than nukes as well as  biochemical warfare and even cyber  attacks are going to allow for some of  the same objectives that nuking a  country might allow for a show of force  an attempt to either attack or or make  political points or whatever show  strength dominance without damaging huge  swathes of land via radiation making  them unusable in addition to the  physical killing of countless people and  in the 21st century in the 22nd century  it increasingly seems to me that those  are going to be the types of warfare  that are fought I mean look at how much  warfare has already changed over the  last 40 years even with the advent of  drone warfare wit and and so many other  technologies that I think it's much more  likely that we would see a dirty bomb  maybe detonated that we would see  biochemical warfare used to the same  crippling effect as a nuclear weapon  conceivably could but I see the  continued use of nukes to say look we  have nukes you can't nuke us but it's  hard to imagine a nation going so rogue  that they say we're going to destroy a  huge part of the world now you may hear  me say this and say David that's exactly  what people thought before the u.s.  twice used nuclear weapons and I agree  with you and I may well be wrong in 50  years this video we may watch it and say  boy how wrong was David but I think it's  more likely that we will see the  offensive you  of biochemical attacks potentially a  dirty bomb and cyber if you disagree  with me let me know we've got a great  bonus show for you today and so much  other great stuff happening next week
 

